1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,500
This is OutcomeLoop: an autonomous,
governed controller for voice agents.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,500
It watches pickup and engagement
and tests better welcomes and voices.

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:14,500
It asks the client for approval,
applies it, and backs out when needed.

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:19,500
Of fifteen capabilities: eleven built,
three partly built, one cut.

5
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:24,500
The cut one: fair sharing of credits
across tenants.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
One Python process, one SQLite file.
Dependencies: httpx and numpy.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
The simulator moves only when we advance,
so the loop is synchronous.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Every 15 minutes: poll approvals,
apply what was approved.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:46,000
On the hour, per workflow: caller ID,
hallucination checks, experiments.

10
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Then a desired config, compared with
the live one, routed through governance.

11
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Then advance the clock and ingest events,
one transaction per chunk.

12
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,500
Everything that matters lives
in that one SQLite file.

13
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
A real run: baseline, simulator,
then our controller through run.sh.

14
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
It logs one line per simulated day.

15
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Now a finished run of the
incidents scenario.

16
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:26,000
status reads only our database:
events, throughput, credits, alerts.

17
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:31,000
One hallucination incident, one decay
rollback, nothing in an uncertain state.

18
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Day 3, 11:30: a Kestrel supervisor
ships prompt P2.

19
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Fifteen minutes later our validation
probe fails it.

20
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:49,000
A known-good prompt from our own
history passes validation.

21
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,000
One prompt-only approval request
goes out.

22
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:59,500
Applied at 13:30, verified that evening.

23
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Nothing changes on a client's agent
without passing governance.

24
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Each request is written to SQLite
before it is sent.

25
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,000
One open request per workflow;
everything else is batched into it.

26
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
We send only if the slowest reply
still lands before expiry.

27
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:26,000
These hold records are the controller
choosing to wait.

28
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Approver hours, expiry timing, fatigue
with an incident slot, cool-downs.

29
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Caller ID is auto-applied where policy
allows, in steps within max shift.

30
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Nothing a customer hears
is ever auto-applied.

31
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Experiments are factorial:
60% incumbent, 40% challengers.

32
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:53,000
O'Brien-Fleming alpha budget plus Holm
keeps false winners at 5%.

33
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:59,500
V3 won by about 12%, after guardrail,
cohort and stability checks.

34
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Crash safety rule 1: each chunk commits
with its checkpoint.

35
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Rule 2: every remote write is recorded
as an intent first.

36
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Rule 3: on restart, reconcile
uncertain writes before anything else.

37
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Our harness hard-kills the controller
seven times and verifies the result.

38
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:26,000
No double apply, no lost approval.

39
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:32,000
The review question, answered
from our own store:

40
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:38,000
why did it change at 13:30 on day 3,
and who approved it?

41
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:44,500
Approval id, exact diff, validation
evidence, and what happened next.

42
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:50,000
The grader's reports,
against a no-op baseline.

43
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Development scenario conclusion rate:
+12.5%

44
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Incidents scenario: +24.6%
Unsafe prompt fixed in 105 min

45
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:05,000
The spam-flagged caller ID dropped
to zero share.

46
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Some experiment launches are marked
harmful. Exploring has a cost.

47
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Load: ~41,000 events/s,
42–53 s per simulated day

48
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Memory: 1046 MB
Tests: 199 (197 unit + 2 slow integration)

49
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:29,500
Numbers come from the files in reports/.

50
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:35,000
The limits: experiments optimise
engagement and guard pickup.

51
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:40,000
No welcome-by-voice interaction check.

52
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:46,000
At 10x scale, the single SQLite writer
changes first.

53
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Next: Postgres partitions and
workers sharded by workflow.

54
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Everything runs from the README,
one script per scenario.

55
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:59,500
Thank you.
